\n" [:option {:value "350234"} "Ski Cross, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350220"} "Halfpipe, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350256"} "Moguls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350263"} "Aerials, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350285"} "Ski Cross, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350271"} "Halfpipe, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350278"} "Slopestyle, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000523"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19020092"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000530"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/1004"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Slopestyle, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "13 February 2014"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/891"} "Ekstrim-Park Rosa Khutor, Krasnaya Polyana"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/350227"} "32 from 15 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Gradient: 23.1°" [:br {}] "Jibbing Features: 3" [:br {}] "Jump Features: 3" [:br {}] "Length: 635 m" [:br {}] "Start Altitude: 1162 m" [:br {}] "Vertical Drop: 147 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Slopestyle was making its Olympic début although it had been contested at the 2011 and 2013 World Championships, and since the early 2000s at the Winter X-Games. Americans were expected to win at least one medal, as they had won 4 of the 6 World Championships medals, held 4 of the top 6 spots at the recent X-Games, and neither of their two World Champions could even make the US team. No one was a expecting a medal sweep, but USA skiiers did exactly that."] "\n\n" [:p {} "High temperatures created soft, slushy conditions. " [:a {:href "/athletes/128709"} "Joss Christensen"] " won the gold medal with a near-perfect first run in the finals, followed by his teammates " [:a {:href "/athletes/128712"} "Gus Kenworthy"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128711"} "Nick Goepper"] ". All three landed a triple corked spin. Christensen’s gold was more impressive as he was the last skiier to make the US team for the event, being added only after winning a late qualifying event. His winning run saw him perform a switch slide to an inverted 450 off the final box feature, and a jump section that included a double corked 1260 with a double Japan grab, a switch right-side double corked 1080 with a tail grab, and a switch triple corked 1260 with a Japan grab."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Goepper had won the recent X-Games (and the 2013 event) and was the gold medal favorite, having also won a bronze medal at the 2013 Worlds. The medal sweep for the USA was only the third one ever at the Winter Olympics, after " [:a {:href "/results/12968"} "1956 men’s figure skating"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/1657"} "2002 men’s snowboarding halfpipe"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "34"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128709"} "Joss Christensen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "93.20 (1)"] [:td {} "95.80 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128712"} "Gus Kenworthy"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countri